# Generated output. `site/` is rendered from `content/` in about a second, so
# committing it would double the repository to store something reproducible —
# and every restyle would show up as a diff across 271 files.
site/
site-banners/

# NOT ignored, deliberately: `content/` and `recovered/`.
#
# `content/` is generated, but it is the product — the Markdown archive is the
# thing people download and reuse, so it is committed along with its images
# and PDFs.
#
# `recovered/` is an INPUT, and the only one that is not reproducible: those
# files came from Wayback Machine snapshots of a domain that now returns 503.
# Losing them would mean losing the figures again, so they and their manifest
# are committed.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Session artefacts of the development protocol: process, not product.
.dev-protocol/plans/

# Local development scaffolding — the dev-protocol's instructions, doc checker,
# spec registry and probe template. Process for whoever is working on this copy,
# not part of the journal or its tooling, so it is kept out of the public repo.
CLAUDE.md
.scripts/
docs/SPECS.md
proofs/README.md
proofs/example.mjs
